        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the inpatient treatment of your 73-year-old female patient, admitted on 05/06/2025 due to an acute exacerbation of known COPD. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. She was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout the stay. Under this regimen, her condition improved satisfactorily, and she was discharged in a stable condition on 06/06/2025. I recommend continuation of her bronchodilator therapy and close outpatient monitoring of her pulmonary function. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
